IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lpula-practice`
IMPORT `lpula-costs`
IMPORT `lpula-qa`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (lpula-qa.l4): every exported
-- question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed
-- term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value of that input under
-- which it does not arise, the situation inputs before it given values under which they hold, and every later input
-- ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the lawyer (the baseline's seat) each question's answer is also asserted
-- equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. The client's answers are worked by hand from the text;
-- mirror cases ask d038 from both seats.
--
-- Not every "not read" claim rests on a case. The situation inputs are read only as BOOLEANs or through helpers that
-- list every value with no OTHERWISE, so an ASSUMEd value read there fails. The baseline reads some enumerations
-- through CONSIDER ... OTHERWISE or EQUALS, and its records only through fields; for those the order of the checks is
-- shown by the parameter script and the code as well as by the cases (graffiti D8.8).
--
-- Facts: Daniel's d023, d031 and d038, and the baseline's fixtures, copied from lpula-cases-practice.l4 and
-- lpula-cases-costs.l4 (a case file cannot be imported without running its assertions). The renewal periods are the
-- baseline's HYPOTHETICAL ones. Expected values are written by hand from the deposited text, never copied from the
-- output.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked Forum` IS A Forum
ASSUME `an unasked Title` IS A Title
ASSUME `an unasked Costs agreement so far` IS A `Costs agreement so far`
ASSUME `an unasked How I did my PLT` IS A `How I did my PLT`
ASSUME `an unasked My admission application` IS A `My admission application`
ASSUME `an unasked My certificate application` IS A `My certificate application`
ASSUME `an unasked My conditional costs agreement` IS A `My conditional costs agreement`
ASSUME `an unasked My costs position` IS A `My costs position`
ASSUME `an unasked My law course` IS A `My law course`
ASSUME `an unasked My matter` IS A `My matter`
ASSUME `an unasked My practical legal training` IS A `My practical legal training`
ASSUME `an unasked My standing` IS A `My standing`
ASSUME `an unasked PLT form` IS A `PLT form`
ASSUME `an unasked What I want decided` IS A `What I want decided`
ASSUME `an unasked What I want to do` IS A `What I want to do`

`as the lawyer` MEANS `I am studying law, seeking admission, or practising as a lawyer in WA`
`as the client` MEANS `I am a client of a law practice, or am thinking of instructing one`

`no agreement` MEANS `there is no costs agreement`
`not conditional` MEANS `a costs agreement that is not a conditional costs agreement`
`a conditional` MEANS `a conditional costs agreement`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's)`


